    "pronunciation": "\"vowel\": English has many more vowel sounds than its five vowel letters, and one letter can stand for several sounds (the **a** in *cat*, *cake*, and *father*). Learners whose language has fewer vowels often merge pairs such as *ship* and *sheep*."
